cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "A regular Hadamard matrix of order 4·933²"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/regular-hadamard-933"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/regular-hadamard-933"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A paper and release repository giving a regular Hadamard matrix of order
  4·933^2 = 3481956, with every row and column sum 1866; the Menon parameter
  933 = 3·311 was listed as undecided in 2007 and 2018. The main tool is a
  completion theorem: four functions on the plane F_q^2, q = 3 mod 4, each a
  constant sign or a sign times the quadratic character on every punctured
  line, can be completed to four disjoint T-matrices with row sums (q,0,0,0)
  exactly when each line carries two character rows, each row has an odd
  number of constant lines, and the character sums have energy 2q at every
  frequency. Applied to the half-lines of Leung, Ma and Schmidt at q = 311,
  this gives the T-matrices, and a nine-point factor and the Goethals-Seidel
  array give the matrix. Published product theorems give infinite families of
  regular parameters 311r and 311rm^2. One fixed set of four sign words works
  at exactly the primes p = 7 mod 16 satisfying three quadratic equations, a
  set with O(log X) members up to X. Novelty is bounded to the sources
  searched.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - regular Hadamard matrices
  - Menon designs
  - symmetric designs
  - T-matrices
  - cyclotomy
